  51:     - Put a green marker in the center of the top row, then trace the glyphs downward: a vertical glyph paints two red cells in the current column; an elbow paints the two bottom cells as a horizontal red segment and moves the current column left or right.
  52:     Key insight
  53:     - The missing top cell of each 2x2 elbow tells whether the trace exits left or right; the glyphs are pipe instructions rather than shapes to copy literally.
